{{!-- /the-faith-received/pins/ — the research portfolio.

     ROUTING. routes.yaml must map this template at
     /the-faith-received/pins/. The deploy Action does NOT ship
     routes.yaml (FRONTEND §6.12); until it is uploaded by hand this URL
     404s however healthy the template is.

     PORTED from the corpus owner's /pins. His structure is kept:
     collections as tabs, a memo under them, cards in the reader's own
     order, relations drawn between two pins and shown as a
     constellation, and an export. His chrome is not.

     ONE NOTEBOOK, SEEN AS COLLECTIONS. The passages are the same ones
     the reader's own notebook panel holds — window.MOFaithNotebook,
     assets/js/lib/faith-notebook-store.js. This page never copies them.
     window.MOFaithCollections (assets/js/lib/faith-collections-store.js)
     owns only the GROUPING: a name, a memo, an ordered list of entry
     ids, and the relations between them. Read that store's header
     before changing anything here; the reasoning for holding ids rather
     than records is the whole design.

     Because the grouping is separate, a passage kept while reading
     appears here immediately under "Not in a collection" without having
     been filed. That group is a view, not a stored collection, and it
     is only offered when it has something in it.

     DOM contract for assets/js/page/faith-pins.js. Every selector in
     that file:
       - [data-pins-root] wrapping everything
       - [data-pins-tabs] — the collection strip
       - [data-pins-count], [data-pins-status]
       - [data-pins-memo] wrapping a textarea
       - [data-pins-bar] holding [data-pins-new], [data-pins-rename],
         [data-pins-delete], [data-pins-group], [data-pins-link],
         [data-pins-rel] (the relation vocabulary)
       - [data-pins-name-form] > [data-pins-name-legend],
         [data-pins-name-input], [data-pins-name-cancel]
       - [data-pins-list] — the cards, each [data-pins-id]
       - [data-pins-constellation]
       - [data-pins-foot] holding [data-pins-copy], [data-pins-download],
         [data-pins-share]

     Remove is TWO PRESSES on the collection, matching
     _notebook-panel.hbs and for the same reason: someone's own
     arrangement, no undo. Removing a passage FROM a collection is one
     press, because that one is reversible — the passage stays in the
     notebook and can be filed again. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-feature">

  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="/the-faith-received/pins/">Pins</a></p>
      <h1>Pins</h1>
      <p class="bhero-sub">The passages you have kept, gathered into collections, with the relations between them drawn out.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bband faith-feature-body faith-pins-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="research-workspace">
        <div class="research-workspace-inner" data-pins-root>

          <div class="pins-tabs" data-pins-tabs role="tablist" aria-label="Your collections"></div>

          <div class="pins-head">
            <p class="pins-count" data-pins-count hidden></p>
            <div class="pins-bar" data-pins-bar hidden>
              <button type="button" class="pins-act" data-pins-new>New collection</button>
              <button type="button" class="pins-act" data-pins-rename>Rename</button>
              <button type="button" class="pins-act" data-pins-group aria-pressed="false">Group by author</button>
              <button type="button" class="pins-act" data-pins-link aria-pressed="false">Draw a relation</button>
              <label class="pins-rel-field">
                <span class="visually-hidden">How the first passage relates to the second</span>
                <select class="pins-rel" data-pins-rel>
                  <option value="parallels">parallels</option>
                  <option value="supports">supports</option>
                  <option value="contests">contests</option>
                  <option value="cites">cites</option>
                  <option value="expands">expands</option>
                </select>
              </label>
              <button type="button" class="pins-act pins-act-danger" data-pins-delete>Delete collection</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          {{!-- A real form rather than window.prompt(), which the
                original used: prompt cannot be styled, is invisible to
                the flow of the page for a screen reader, and is blocked
                outright in some embedded browsers, where the button
                would simply appear to do nothing. --}}
          <form class="pins-name-form" data-pins-name-form hidden>
            <label class="pins-name-label">
              <span data-pins-name-legend>Name the new collection</span>
              <input type="text" class="pins-name-input" data-pins-name-input maxlength="60" autocomplete="off" />
            </label>
            <button type="submit" class="pins-act pins-act-primary">Save</button>
            <button type="button" class="pins-act" data-pins-name-cancel>Cancel</button>
          </form>

          <p class="pins-status" data-pins-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

          {{!-- Working notes for the collection as a whole, distinct
                from the note on any one passage. Saved on blur: this
                writes the whole store back, and doing that per
                keystroke is a stutter on a phone. --}}
          <div class="pins-memo" data-pins-memo hidden>
            <label class="pins-memo-label" for="pins-memo-text">Working notes for this collection</label>
            <textarea id="pins-memo-text" class="pins-memo-text" rows="3" placeholder="What you are assembling here, and why&hellip;"></textarea>
          </div>

          <div class="pins-list" data-pins-list></div>

          <div class="pins-constellation" data-pins-constellation></div>

          <div class="pins-foot" data-pins-foot hidden>
            <div class="pins-foot-acts">
              <button type="button" class="pins-act" data-pins-copy>Copy as Markdown</button>
              <button type="button" class="pins-act" data-pins-download>Download</button>
              <button type="button" class="pins-act" data-pins-share>Share as a link</button>
            </div>
            <p class="pins-foot-note">Kept in this browser only. Copy or download anything you want to keep. A share link carries the passages and the relations between them, not your working notes.</p>
            <p class="pins-foot-note"><a href="/the-faith-received/desk/">Open the Desk</a> to write from a collection, or <a href="/the-faith-received/compare/">Compare</a> two authors on a topic.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
{{> "membership-cta"}}

{{!-- The notebook store FIRST, then the collections store, which reads
     MOFaithNotebook.RELATIONS on its first pass, then the page script,
     which needs both. Page-template scripts run BEFORE site.min.js
     (FRONTEND §6.18); the only bundle global any of these touches is
     window.MOSafeHref, which ships in boot.min.js in <head>. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/lib/faith-notebook-store.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/lib/faith-collections-store.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-pins.js"}}"></script>
